<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Exploring My Community – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em; margin-top: 5px;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 2nd Grade (CEFR: Pre-A1.4)</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Exploring My Community</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> It's the Market!</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Text: Connect ideas from a text with personal experiences. Concept: Show a connection between class concepts and personal experiences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can connect ideas from a text with personal experiences by pointing to images (e.g., points to a market picture and says, "I go there on the weekend."). Can show a connection between class concepts and personal experiences by drawing familiar places (e.g., draw a park to show "my favorite place"). Can relate new vocabulary to familiar places by pointing and naming (e.g., points to "school" and says "I go to school.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher greets students, "Good morning, everyone! Let's talk about our community places." The teacher holds up flashcards of community places (park, market, school, church, store, home). Students chorally name the places. Teacher asks, "Where do you go?" and students point to the correct flashcard or say the word (e.g., "market"). The teacher says, "Today, we will tell about our places."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher shows a picture of a market from a story previously read. Teacher points to the market and says, "It's the market. I go to the market." The teacher then points to a picture of a park and says, "It's a big park. I play in the park." The teacher emphasizes /p/ in "park" and /m/ in "market." The teacher models connecting information by saying, "This picture shows the market. I know the market. My mom goes to the market."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher points to a market picture: "Is this a school or a market?" (Expected answer: "Market!")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher says, "I go to the market." Then asks, "Do I stay home?" (Expected answer: "No!")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>Input of new language/content</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Exploring My Community".</b> The teacher presents a simple, large poster or projected image of a local community map with labeled places (park, market, school, church, library, store). Each place has a very short descriptive sentence next to it, like: "This is the market. It is busy." or "This is the school. I go here."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Illustrated community map with short descriptive sentences (e.g., "It's the market. It's busy."). Genre: Informational map/picture story. Register: Simple and descriptive. Format: Large poster or digital projection.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Describing places and activities: "The park is big. I play there." Answering questions: "Where is the library?" "Next to the market."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> Teacher points to the map: "What do we see?" (Expected answer: "Places!" or "Market! Park!")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching (TPR):</b> Teacher says, "Point to the school!" Students point to the school on the map. Teacher says, "Where is the market?" Students point and say, "Here!"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-9 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>Accuracy focus</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Accuracy focus on Mediation.</b> Students practice connecting descriptions to places and relating them to their own experiences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> WH-questions ("Where is it?"), Present simple ("It's the market."), Adjectives + nouns ("big park").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> park, market, school, library, church, store, home, go, play, big, small, busy, in, on, next to.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Focus on /p/ in "park" and /m/ in "market".</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled practice (Picture-Sentence Matching):</b> The teacher provides students with individual worksheets or flashcards. Each card has a picture of a community place (e.g., a park) and a separate card with a simple sentence description (e.g., "It's a big park."). Students match the picture to its description. The teacher checks understanding by asking, "What place is this?" and "What does it say?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-controlled practice (Listen and Point/Say):</b> The teacher reads aloud a simple sentence describing a place from the community map (e.g., "It's the market. It is busy."). Students point to the market on their individual community map. Then, the teacher asks, "Do you go to the market?" Students respond with "Yes, I go." or "No, I don't." or "My market is big." Teacher encourages initial sound identification for /ch/ in "church."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Interaction (Connect and Share):</b> In pairs, students take turns picking a flashcard of a community place. Student A shows the picture (e.g., "school") and says, "This is the school." Student B then connects it to personal experience by saying, "My school is (big/small)." or "I go to school." The teacher circulates, facilitating and correcting pronunciation and grammar, especially polite expressions like "Excuse me, where is the library?" for location questions.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>Communicative task</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Exploring My Community".</b> This stage focuses on the 21st Century Skills Project: "Community Place Scavenger Hunt."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Scavenger Hunt and mini-presentation/explanation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Setup:</b> The teacher places large pictures of community places (park, market, school, library, church, store) around the classroom. Separate descriptive cards (e.g., "It's the market. It is busy.") are placed in a central basket.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Scavenger Hunt:</b> In small groups, students pick a descriptive card from the basket. They read the description (teacher assists with reading if needed). For example, a group picks "It's a big park. I play there."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Mediation: Connect & Explain:</b> Students then walk around the classroom to find the picture that matches their description. Once they find it, they physically place the description card next to the picture.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. <b>Presentation:</b> Each group points to their matched pair and says, "This is the [place name]." Then they explain how it relates to them personally (e.g., "It's the market. My mom goes there on the weekend." or "It's a big park. I play there. My park is small."). The teacher encourages the use of polite expressions when asking about places ("Excuse me, where is the park?").</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in connecting ideas, collaborative interaction within groups, and successful completion of the scavenger hunt by matching and briefly explaining their connections.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during the scavenger hunt and a simple drawing/labeling task.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Observation (during Scavenger Hunt):</b> The teacher observes students' ability to find the correct picture for the description and their verbal explanation/connection (e.g., pointing to "market" and saying "I go there.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Individual Drawing:</b> Students draw their "favorite place in the community" (e.g., park, home, market) on a small paper. Below the drawing, they attempt to label it (e.g., "park") and draw a simple activity or an object they see there. Teacher asks each student, "What is your favorite place? Why?" (e.g., "It's the park. I play here.").</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Pronounces target words (e.g., park, market, church) clearly.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Uses at least 3-4 community place nouns (e.g., park, market, school) and 1-2 verbs (e.g., go, play).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity in connecting ideas:</b> Can point to a picture/text and relate it to personal experience (e.g., "I go there on the weekend.").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Works with peers during the scavenger hunt.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Point to a place you can tell about."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did you like finding the places?" (Thumbs up/down)</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new place did you talk about today?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Can you tell your family about a place in English?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 20px; padding-left: 0;">
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students connect text/concepts to personal experiences (Mediation)? The scavenger hunt was highly engaging for the age group, and the combination of matching and verbalizing short sentences helped solidify connections. Students enjoyed pointing and drawing their favorite places.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments and scaffolds are needed for next lesson? Some students still need more scaffolding for expressing personal connections beyond single words. Providing sentence starters like "I go to..." or "My [place] is..." more explicitly might help. For the next unit, ensuring a clear progression of vocabulary introduction and usage will be key.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson concludes the "Exploring My Community" theme by integrating all skills and a project. The next lesson will introduce a new theme and set of vocabulary, building on the established routine of introducing places and activities.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-4 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>